.TH MAIL-PROBE 1 "2026-10-16" "SASD Freeware" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mail-probe \- read-only SMTP diagnostic with mandatory verified STARTTLS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mail-probe --host
.I HOST
.RI [ --port\ N ]
.RI [ --timeout\ N ]
.RI [ --ca-file\ ABSOLUTE_PEM ]
.RI [ --null ]
.br
.B mail-probe --help | --version
.SH DESCRIPTION
Checks the SMTP 220 banner, fixed EHLO, STARTTLS advertisement, TLS upgrade
with verified certificate chain and hostname, and post-TLS EHLO. This does
not send or accept messages and does not check deliverability. Only explicit
STARTTLS is supported (default port 587), not implicit TLS on port 465.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --host
Required ASCII DNS name, IDNA A-label or dotted IPv4 address; IPv6 is not
currently supported.
.TP
.B --port
Port 1 through 65535; default 587.
.TP
.B --timeout
Per-phase timeout 1 through 30 seconds; default 5. Overall deadline applies.
.TP
.B --ca-file
Optional absolute regular, readable, non-symlink PEM trust file.
.TP
.B --null
Emit exactly four NUL-terminated fields, no header; see command guide.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
Perl and non-core IO::Socket::SSL 2.009 or newer, working TLS backend and CA
trust. The command itself never executes an external openssl client.
.SH SECURITY
Only EHLO and STARTTLS are sent. No AUTH, MAIL FROM, RCPT TO, DATA,
credentials, queue or server changes, certificate-verification bypass, or
plaintext fallback. Protocol output is limited and validated before printing.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 complete verified STARTTLS dialogue; 1 negative SMTP or TLS result;
2 invalid options; 3 missing dependency, invalid response, or timeout.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR openssl (1)
